4.13 Students are prohibited under the Code of Conduct from using University
facilities, equipment, services or computers without authorization.
4.14 Students are prohibited under the Code of Conduct from forging, altering or
misusing any University document or record.
4.15 Students are prohibited under the Code of Conduct from storing, possessing or
using real or replica firearms or other weapons, explosives (including fireworks),
ammunition, or toxic or otherwise dangerous materials on University premises.
4.16 Students are prohibited under the Code of Conduct from consuming, possessing
or distributing drugs, alcohol or any form of tobacco.
5. Failing to comply with this Code of Conduct will lead to and not limited to:
a) Written warning or reprimand;
b) Payment of costs or compensation for any loss, damage or injury caused by the
conduct;
c) Issuance of an apology, made publicly or privately;
d) Forfeiture of Scholarship, where applicable;
e) Restriction or prohibition of access to, or use of, University facilities, services,
activities or programs;
f) Suspension and or expulsion from the University
